    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gutta Percha used in India-Rubber, Gutta-Percha & Waterproofing: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 637"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "GUTTA-PERCHA: The word \"gutta-percha\" is of Malayan origin : it signifies the gum or gutta or getah of the tree known as percha : according to some writers percha is also the ancient name of Sumatra, so that getah-percha would denote the gutta of Sumatra. And the true gum is to-day almost exclusively a Malayan product. As it reaches the market gutta-percha i..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
